Subject: [PATCH] CRM-27: Agreement Execution Predicate (provider-neutral,
 exactly-once)

- lib/agreements/execution.ts: pure 'is this issued version fully executed?'
  predicate over neutral signature-role evidence + manual/external evidence,
  with a required-role POLICY seam (stop-sign C: default = all declared groups
  required, non-authoritative fixture; NOT a business decision).
- Neutral AGREEMENT_FULLY_EXECUTED DomainEvent type (lib/workflow/contracts.ts).
- db/migrations/067: additive signature_request.execution_role for role-level
  evidence. db/migrations/068: agreement_execution marker (unique doc+version)
  for exactly-once emission.
- db/agreement-execution.ts: claimAgreementExecution (idempotent) +
  getCompletedExecutionRoles evidence reader.
- lib/agreements/completion.ts: compose document -> template -> required roles
  -> completed evidence -> predicate -> exactly-once marker.
- Plumbed optional executionRole through the signature send command/application.
- Reconciliation handler evaluates agreement completion after a neutral
  completed event (backward-compatible, injected, non-fatal).
- Tests: partial/final/manual/optional-vs-required/duplicate replay/wrong
  version; completion exactly-once.
